A||N||15||Elenor84||Tips or techniques for prying axel out of transaxel?||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||09-26-2001||01:32 AM||||Hey guys...I read the hanes manuel but I'm still having trouble...what tool have u guys used to get it out?  Mines an 86Se...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||09-26-2001||01:38 AM||||take a pry-bar between the case and CV housing in the axle - give it a wack||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayUSA77||09-26-2001||01:41 AM||||and when he says wack he means get your grip and do a quick hard pull. It should pop right out. Getting them in is a hole other post!!!<BR>GL<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||09-26-2001||03:48 AM||||Spin the axle with one hand and gently pull the prybar wit the other. Don't force it, just keep spinning it until you get it to its sweet-spot. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||samoht||09-26-2001||07:33 AM||||yep.. I used a big screw driver ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||09-26-2001||09:18 AM||||I used a wooden wedge and it worked great.  The big screw driver and crowbar never worked for me.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||09:20 AM||||I used a prybar and put a 2x.5 piece of wood on the pivot to help protect the trans case.  I didn't hit on it, but used the prybar with just a little bit of slack to 'pop' out the axle.  Works every time. GL||||reg||1
Z||000007||PBJ||09-26-2001||03:21 PM||||I would use two pry bars, one on each side of the tripod and the trans and apply equal pressure and it should pop easily.  A quick jerking action ehh.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Elenor84||09-26-2001||05:24 PM||||wow guys thx very much...!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||09-26-2001||07:10 PM||||I used an 18" prybar and a few wacks of the BFH.  Remember to drain the tranny fluid before you take out the axle!!  I didn't even think about it and got a nice big puddle on my garage floor.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||09-26-2001||07:16 PM||||I broken down and bought the special tool for removing axles. It's essentially a slide hammer with a C shaped plate at the end. <P>There is too much risk to damaging the trans housing and seal on those stuborn axles (or seperating a tri-pot).<P>At the same time, some just snap loose with no effort.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JayUSA77||09-27-2001||01:07 AM||||hey standard you got it easy, i knew a guys that got it all over his face, and he hadnt changed it for god knows how long so it was thick and black.  He Bi#ched for a hour while i lauged for a hour. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">At least i learned from his mistakes<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||Elenor84||09-27-2001||01:51 AM||||Wow this is becoming a big topic...hey guys thx again for your help...I got it out today with about a 2 foot pry bar and just one big wap...!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||87GTZ34||09-27-2001||02:04 AM||||Terry, I bought the axle remover from SPX that sells to GM.  The thing didn't work worth a crap.  I went to the prybar and 2x1/2, pop it came out.  I thought jeez, I wasted my money on that POS tool and the thing just pops out.  Anybody want to buy an axle puller from SPX just like GM techs use?||||reg||1
Z||000014||terryk||09-27-2001||11:28 AM||||I thought Kent Moore supplied GM tools. That's what mine is. <P>Mine works fine, but many axles just about fall out. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||87GTZ34||09-27-2001||12:05 PM||||They do.  I guess they had merged w/ another tool mfg at least 2 yrs ago.  They go by SPX Kent-Moore, heres the link.  <A HREF="http://www.spxkentmoore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.spxkentmoore.com/</A>   Maybe my axle was just tight. Carfax reported only 51 K miles on it before it was wrecked and it is the he '96 heavy duty version.  But slide hammer just bounced on it.  had I had a helper to apply some pressure w/ a bar the hammer probably would have popped it.||||reg||1
